## Context

Child of tracker 1510. The pilot tests the design on the smallest country
before any wider migration: Viet Nam, 58 of the 392 rows of
`data/jetp/documents.csv` (Senegal, the first choice, is the largest at 138).
A pilot on one instance is expected to critique the tracker's design; feed its
findings back into 1510 before filing further children.

## Milestone

M4 (author, 2026-09-29). Do not start before the milestone opens.

## Feasibility (checked 2026-09-29, nothing created)

- Storage and credentials are not blockers. The author has an unlimited
  Zotero Storage plan (group files count against the owner's quota), and the
  read-write key `ZOTERO_RW_API_KEY` in `~/.config/keys/zotero.env` already
  grants `groups.all: library + write`, so it covers a new group with no new
  key (checked via `GET /keys/current`).
- The Web API v3 cannot create a group or change group settings: neither the
  read nor the write documentation has such an endpoint (writable objects are
  items, collections, saved searches, tags, plus file uploads).
- Hence one human step: create the group on zotero.org (Groups, Create a New
  Group) or in the desktop client (File, New Library, New Group), about a
  minute, once. Everything after that is automatable.
- Group type: **PublicClosed**, with file editing for members. Zotero:
  "Open public groups do not allow file sharing", while closed-membership
  public groups can enable it for members only. Non-members see metadata,
  never files; public access to the documents goes through the Web Archive
  snapshots (see 1510). Precedent: the author's existing PublicClosed group
  "Semantic search challenge fixture" is configured this way.
- The pilot then records the new group's numeric ID in the pipeline config,
  not in `.env`.

## Actions

1. Import the Viet Nam documents and every snapshot of each as attachments,
   with `document_id` in Extra and the publisher, date, language and type
   mapped to Zotero fields.
2. Write the export, commit it, and have the D1 reader take Viet Nam rows from
   it instead of `documents.csv`.
3. Verify locator hashes against attachment hashes (confirm that the Web API
   exposes a checksum for each attachment; if it does not, hash the
   downloaded file).
4. Record what did not fit Zotero's model, and in particular whether one
   attachment per byte version stays workable.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The Viet Nam items are in the group library, each with its
      `document_id` in Extra and every snapshot attached.
- [ ] The D2-D4 outputs for Viet Nam are byte-identical before and after
      the switch; the observatory pages differ only in their document links
      (1510 decision 5).
- [ ] A page-level link of the form Web Archive `id_` URL + `#page=N` opens
      the cited page on at least one Viet Nam capture (1510 decision 5).
- [ ] No test and no render calls the Zotero API: builds read the committed
      export, tests read a small fixture export, and `make check-fast` passes
      with the network off.
- [ ] A findings note in the log of 1510: what fits, what does not, go or
      no-go for the other countries.
